  >>> x = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
  >>> y = 1
  >>> tf.add(x, y)
  <tf.Tensor: shape=(5,), dtype=int32, numpy=array([2, 3, 4, 5, 6],
  dtype=int32)>

  Note that binary `+` operator can be used instead:

  >>> x = tf.convert_to_tensor([1, 2, 3, 4, 5])
  >>> y = tf.convert_to_tensor(1)
  >>> x + y
